=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a push-only condition on the pytest step, where push fires only on main, never runs on a pull request
origin: issue #181 sibling — github.event_name is bound to each event that can run the workflow
origin2: on a pull request's commits; here that is pull_request alone, and the condition is false for it.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
        if: github.event_name == 'push'
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["CI_TEST_COMMAND_WEAKENED"]}]
